  {
   "id": "OKfjtVPWBgAJ",
   "from": "Eric Rexstad",
   "author": "75e0b0abcbafbc7d",
   "date": "2023-10-16T15:58:14Z",
   "subject": "Re: [distance-sampling] How to enter the data of my census.",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nHello Gustavo, welcome to the group.</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nLet me know if I have misunderstood any of this, but here is how I understand your survey design.</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nSix vegetation types (you are referring to these as &quot;sites&quot;) and you wish to have an estimate of bird abundance or density for each vegetation type.</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nIf this is accurate, I would create a table or spreadsheet of data in this manner:</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nStudy area - one name (Patagonia)</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nRegion - six vegetation types</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nPoint transect - name of point</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nObservation (distance) - midpoint of bin in which detection was made (0-10m=5, 10-20m=15, 20-30m=25,...)</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nThere is a sample project that ships with Distance for Windows (in the folder Sample Projects) that resembles your study. It is called &quot;House Wren&quot; and is a study of\r\n<i>Troglodytes aedon </i>in the western U.S.  The data in Distance for Windows looks like this:</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<img style=\"max-width:100%\" size=\"41098\" src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/distance-sampling/attach/6d653b5e3a738/image.png?part=0.1&amp;view=1\"></div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n&quot;Study area&quot; would be as I describe above, you would not need the &quot;Visits&quot; column as you will provide that in the &quot;Survey effort&quot; column later. Your first region label could be &quot;Ñire open Forest&quot; and the associate size of this vegetation type. Your points could\r\n be labelled anything that makes sense to you, and Survey effort would be the number of visits to the point (3 I think you said). Finally the Radial distance would be the midpoint of your distance bands. You would not need the final &quot;Observer&quot; column as in\r\n the house wren data.</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nNote, the number of transects is three or four as you noted, not three or four multiplied by the number of visits (which is how I suspect you arrived at the number 12 in your note).</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nI hope this is helpful.<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div></div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<hr style=\"display:inline-block;width:98%\">\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\"><font face=\"Calibri, sans-serif\" style=\"font-size:11pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><b>From:</b> <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">distance...@googlegroups.com</a> &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">distance...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt; on behalf of Gustavo Iglesias &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">gjigl...@gmail.com</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Sent:</b> 16 October 2023 16:00<br>\r\n<b>To:</b> distance-sampling &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">distance...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Subject:</b> [distance-sampling] How to enter the data of my census.</font>\r\n<div> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Dear all:\r\n<div><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>This is the first time I´m in touch with the group. I was reading the manuals and videos about distance software but up to date I couldn´t understand well how can I enter my data. Perhaps it´s becuse english is not my language and probably I missed the\r\n meaning of some words and concepts.</div>\r\n<div><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>To summarise my data has the following characteristicas:</div>\r\n<div><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>6 vegetation types sampled</li><li>On each site I used point transect methods.</li><li>On each vegattion type I censused bird on three or four points separated each other 100 meters.</li><li>I repeated the census  for three consecutive days</li><li>I sampled all birds seen or heard and estimate the distance (meters) to me.</li><li>The time on each point was 10 minutes.</li><li>After the census  I grouped the data in 10-meter interevals.</li></ul>\r\n<div>It was difficult for me to assign these data and values to the fields defined by Distance i.e.: Study area - Region - Point Transect - Observation.</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>For example One of my vegetation type was: </div>\r\n<div>Ñire open Forest (the study was done on Patagonian Andean Forest ion Argentina)</div>\r\n<div>12 points censused.</div>\r\n<div>data grouped in 10-meter bands.</div>\r\n<div><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div><span border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" width=\"223\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse;width:168pt\"><span width=\"133\" style=\"width:100pt\"></span><span width=\"90\" style=\"width:68pt\"></span><span height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15pt\"><span colspan=\"2\" height=\"20\" width=\"223\" style=\"min-height:15pt;width:168pt\"><span border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" width=\"223\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse;width:168pt\"><span width=\"133\" style=\"width:100pt\"></span><span width=\"90\" style=\"width:68pt\"></span><span height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15pt\"><span colspan=\"2\" height=\"20\" width=\"223\" style=\"min-height:15pt;width:168pt\"><br>\r\nÑire Open Forest</span></span><span height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15pt\"><span height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15pt;border-top:none\"><br>\r\nBand   Nr. of BIrds</span><span style=\"border-top:none;border-left:none\"><br>\r\n</span></span><span height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15pt\"><span height=\"20\" align=\"right\" style=\"min-height:15pt;border-top:none\">10            34</span><span align=\"right\" style=\"border-top:none;border-left:none\"><br>\r\n</span></span><span height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15pt\"><span height=\"20\" align=\"right\" style=\"min-height:15pt;border-top:none\"><br>\r\n20            80</span><span align=\"right\" style=\"border-top:none;border-left:none\"><br>\r\n</span></span><span height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15pt\"><span height=\"20\" align=\"right\" style=\"min-height:15pt;border-top:none\"><br>\r\n30            52 </span><span align=\"right\" style=\"border-top:none;border-left:none\"><br>\r\n</span></span><span height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15pt\"><span height=\"20\" align=\"right\" style=\"min-height:15pt;border-top:none\"><br>\r\n40            17</span><span align=\"right\" style=\"border-top:none;border-left:none\"><br>\r\n</span></span><span height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15pt\"><span height=\"20\" align=\"right\" style=\"min-height:15pt;border-top:none\"><br>\r\n50              3</span><span align=\"right\" style=\"border-top:none;border-left:none\"><br>\r\n</span></span><span height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15pt\"><span height=\"20\" align=\"right\" style=\"min-height:15pt;border-top:none\"><br>\r\n60              6</span><span align=\"right\" style=\"border-top:none;border-left:none\"><br>\r\n</span></span><span height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15pt\"><span height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15pt;border-top:none\"><br>\r\nTOTAL    1</span><span align=\"right\" style=\"border-top:none;border-left:none\">92</span>\r\n</span></span><br>\r\n</span></span></span></div>\r\n<div><span border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" width=\"223\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse;width:168pt\"><span height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15pt\"><span colspan=\"2\" height=\"20\" width=\"223\" style=\"min-height:15pt;width:168pt\"><span border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" width=\"223\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse;width:168pt\"><span height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15pt\"><span align=\"right\" style=\"border-top:none;border-left:none\"><br>\r\n</span></span></span></span></span></span></div>\r\n<div><span border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" width=\"223\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse;width:168pt\"><span height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15pt\"><span colspan=\"2\" height=\"20\" width=\"223\" style=\"min-height:15pt;width:168pt\"><span border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" width=\"223\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse;width:168pt\"><span height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15pt\"><span align=\"right\" style=\"border-top:none;border-left:none\">I\r\n hope my questions are clear and I really thanks any help you can give.</span></span></span></span></span></span></div>\r\n<div><span border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" width=\"223\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse;width:168pt\"><span height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15pt\"><span colspan=\"2\" height=\"20\" width=\"223\" style=\"min-height:15pt;width:168pt\"><span border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" width=\"223\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse;width:168pt\"><span height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15pt\"><span align=\"right\" style=\"border-top:none;border-left:none\"><br>\r\n</span></span></span></span></span></span></div>\r\n<div><span border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" width=\"223\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse;width:168pt\"><span height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15pt\"><span colspan=\"2\" height=\"20\" width=\"223\" style=\"min-height:15pt;width